size_flags_vertical = 3
theme = ExtResource("6_ar0mo")
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 25
text = "Not all Video Containers and Codecs are supported.

Generally most MP4's will work fine.
Some MOV's work.

More testing is needed to determine what containers and codecs play properly.
Videos containing more than 2 Audio channels will not play the audio from any additional channels.
This mainly pertains to Surround Sound encoded Audio."
horizontal_alignment = 1
autowrap_mode = 2

[node name="HelpPlaylistText" type="VBoxContainer" parent="GuiMargin/GUI/Main/PlaylistPanel/SettingsPopup/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer/MarginContainer2/HBoxContainer/Panel2/SettingsOptions/InfoDocumentation/VBoxContainer2/ScrollContainer/HelpTexts"]
unique_name_in_owner = true
layout_mode = 2

[node name="HelpPlaylistText1" type="Label" parent="GuiMargin/GUI/Main/PlaylistPanel/SettingsPopup/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer/MarginContainer2/HBoxContainer/Panel2/SettingsOptions/InfoDocumentation/VBoxContainer2/ScrollContainer/HelpTexts/HelpPlaylistText"]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(220, 0)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme = ExtResource("6_ar0mo")
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 25
text = "
You can save a playlist you have setup, it will retain all the individual settings data saved in the individual items.

Playslists are bundled together into one folder along with the playlist.exvp file.
All files added to your playlist will copied into one location for easy transfering between systems.
When you press SAVE, you choose or create the folder where everything will be stored.
"
horizontal_alignment = 1
autowrap_mode = 2

[node name="Tree" type="Tree" parent="GuiMargin/GUI/Main/PlaylistPanel/SettingsPopup/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer/MarginContainer2/HBoxContainer/Panel2/SettingsOptions/InfoDocumentation/VBoxContainer2/ScrollContainer/HelpTexts/HelpPlaylistText"]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(400, 550)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 4
focus_mode = 0
allow_search = false
hide_folding = true
enable_recursive_folding = false
scroll_horizontal_enabled = false
scroll_vertical_enabled = false
script = ExtResource("18_2cgqg")

[node name="HelpPlaylistText3" type="Label" parent="GuiMargin/GUI/Main/PlaylistPanel/SettingsPopup/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer/MarginContainer2/HBoxContainer/Panel2/SettingsOptions/InfoDocumentation/VBoxContainer2/ScrollContainer/HelpTexts/HelpPlaylistText"]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(220, 0)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme = ExtResource("6_ar0mo")
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 25
text = "
Removing a playlist item from the queue and then saving will remove the corresponding file from the bundle location

You can either press the load button to navigate to the playlist file, or you can drag and drop the exvp file into the program.

The playlist Items can be reordered without interupting playback.

Tip:
Right click the .exvp file in your file explorer and set to always open with the EXVP.exe to quickly launch playlists from File Explorer.

"
horizontal_alignment = 1
autowrap_mode = 2

[node name="HelpTrimText" type="Label" parent="GuiMargin/GUI/Main/PlaylistPanel/SettingsPopup/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer/MarginContainer2/HBoxContainer/Panel2/SettingsOptions/InfoDocumentation/VBoxContainer2/ScrollContainer/HelpTexts"]
unique_name_in_owner = true
visible = false
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(220, 0)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme = ExtResource("6_ar0mo")
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 25
text = "
In the Video item settings panel, drag the green Start Handle and the Red End handle to where you would like the video to start and end at.

You can hold key modifiers to adjust the handle positions more precisely.
Hold the following key modifiers while dragging to adjust the position in the following increments:

DRAG + CTRL:           1 Sec
DRAG + SHIFT:          10 Sec 
DRAG + CTRL + SHIFT:   60 Sec

Right Click the handles to set them back to their last saved positions

Upon making changes press the save button to lock in the new in and out times."
horizontal_alignment = 1
autowrap_mode = 2

[node name="HelpSlideshows" type="Label" parent="GuiMargin/GUI/Main/PlaylistPanel/SettingsPopup/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer/MarginContainer2/HBoxContainer/Panel2/SettingsOptions/InfoDocumentation/VBoxContainer2/ScrollContainer/HelpTexts"]
unique_name_in_owner = true
visible = false
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(220, 0)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme = ExtResource("6_ar0mo")
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 25
text = "
Drag and drop a folder containing images into the Program and it will auto generate a Basic Slideshow with fade transitions.

After selecting a Slideshow from the Playlist, you can scroll, hover and select a picture to skip to.

Picture order can be shuffled via the button in the item settings, or individual pictures can be dragged and dropped into different orders.

*for now, the only transition type is a crossfade*"
horizontal_alignment = 1
autowrap_mode = 2

[node name="HelpShortcuts" type="Label" parent="GuiMargin/GUI/Main/PlaylistPanel/SettingsPopup/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer/MarginContainer2/HBoxContainer/Panel2/SettingsOptions/InfoDocumentation/VBoxContainer2/ScrollContainer/HelpTexts"]
unique_name_in_owner = true
visible = false
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(220, 0)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme = ExtResource("6_ar0mo")
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 25
text = "
\"Space\" - Play/Pause selected video/slideshow

\"Left/Right\" - Backwards/Forwards 1 second

\"Shift + Left/Right\" - Backwards/Forwards 10 seconds

\"Ctrl + Shift + Left/Right\" - Backwards/Forwards 60 seconds

\"Ctrl + Shift + Alt + X\" - Close Extended Output"
horizontal_alignment = 1
autowrap_mode = 2

[node name="HelpCompanionText" type="Label" parent="GuiMargin/GUI/Main/PlaylistPanel/SettingsPopup/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer/MarginContainer2/HBoxContainer/Panel2/SettingsOptions/InfoDocumentation/VBoxContainer2/ScrollContainer/HelpTexts"]
unique_name_in_owner = true
visible = false
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(220, 0)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme = ExtResource("6_ar0mo")
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 25
text = "
Manual Companion Support can be configured:
In options under Network, Enable EXVP Listen (Receives Commands from Companion) and choose your Address and Port or leave at default.
The Companion Address should be set to whatever Companion is set to (Sends Playback Time and Time Remaining to Companion).

In companion setup a new Generic: HTTP Requests connection. Under Base URL, enter the address in your EXVP Listen Parameter at the top of this window and name the connection label EXVP and save the Connection.

Create a new button and under Press Actions, pick EXVP from the Browse Menu, then select POST. URL stays Blank.
Set Content Type to \"text/plain\". Under Body, enter the command you want to send to EXVP. Then Name your button Accordingly.

The List of supported commands are: 

play - Toggle this to play/ pause 
previous, next - selects the corresponding video in the playlist
VolUp, VolDown - adjust the volume of the selected video
SetIn, SetOut - Set trim points for the selected video

For Live In and Out Playback Times, Create 2 new buttons and set their title to \"In:\\n$(internal:custom_EXVP_In)\" and \"Out:\\n$(internal:custom_EXVP_Out)\".
NOTE: you must include the brackets and dollar signs.
Under the Tab titled \"$ Variables\", add 2 new custom variables to companion called \"EXVP_In\" and \"EXVP_Out\"

They will now live update when a video is selected and playing"
horizontal_alignment = 1
autowrap_mode = 2

